# Cloudflare Pages SPA fallback.
#
# Only used if this is deployed as a classic Pages project. The live deploy is
# a Workers static-assets project, where the same job is done by
# `not_found_handling: "single-page-application"` in wrangler.jsonc. Kept
# because it costs nothing and makes the Pages path work without edits.
#
# Every route on this site is client-side: /components/s3 is a React Router
# match, not a file on disk. Without this line a hard refresh or an inbound
# link to anything other than / returns Pages' own 404, which is the single
# most common way a working SPA looks broken the moment it is deployed.
#
# 200 (not 301) matters: the URL stays as the reader typed it and the router
# reads it, rather than the browser being sent home.
/*    /index.html   200
